{
    "background_story": "Fabian was a charming pastry chef with a passion for creating exquisite desserts. Growing up in a small village in France, he was surrounded by the rich aromas of freshly baked bread and pastries. His love affair with hazelnuts began when he discovered his grandmother's secret recipe for hazelnut praline cake. The nutty flavor and crunchy texture captivated his senses, and he spent years perfecting his own hazelnut creations. Fabian's bakery, 'Le Coeur de la Noisette' (The Heart of the Hazelnut), quickly gained a loyal following for its signature hazelnut croissants, cakes, and chocolates. His dedication to using only the finest hazelnuts from local farmers earned him a reputation as a master artisan. Fabian's love for hazelnuts was more than just a flavor preference \u2013 it was a connection to his heritage and a way to share joy with his community.",
